A||||5||88formula||Have a question about the KYB front shocks. ||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||06-03-2001||04:08 PM||||I have the front KYB GR-2 shocks. I noticed that compared to my original shocks they extend out on their own. I measured the amount of force they extend out with and I got 17.4 lbs. That means that they will be lifting the front of the car with a total force of 34.8 lbs. Did anyone notice that after installing these shocks that their front ends where higher off the ground because of this? <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||06-03-2001||05:37 PM||||Yep.  I just put KYB's all around on my GT about a month or so ago.  any high-pressure shocks will do that.  The original shocks should have held up the front end when they were new, but after 15 years mine were completely blown.  I think the ride improvement is more than worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||06-03-2001||06:13 PM||||I got the white HD KYB's on mine with lowering springs. They held the front end back up to stock ride height for a couple days and about a dozen passes over speed bumps. After that they settled down nicely. Pic in my sig is with them on.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||06-03-2001||06:36 PM||||I replaced the (still good) OEM replacement shocks in my 84 with the white KYB, and they were more or less the same height. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-03-2001||09:38 PM||||Well the stock shocks I have are still good and they don't extend out on there own. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sjp777||06-03-2001||09:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Well the stock shocks I have are still good and they don't extend out on there own. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Then the stock ones either weren't gas charged to begin with, or they have long since lost pressure.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
